    "replacement": "{bpm: 120} {time: 4/4} {key: G}\n\n// Complete American Notation Reference\n// Shakespeare's \"A Midsummer Night's Dream\" meets jazz harmony\n\n// ===== BASIC TRIADS & SEVENTHS =====\n{label: intro}\nG           D           Em          C           // Major, minor triads\nI know a bank where the wild thyme blows,\nGmaj7       Am7         Bm7         Cmaj7       // Major 7th, minor 7th\nWhere oxlips and the nodding violet grows.\n\n// ===== SLASH CHORDS (Inversions) =====\nG/B         C/E         D/F#        G/D\nQuite over-canopied with luscious woodbine,\nAm/C        D/A         G/B         C\nWith sweet musk-roses and with eglantine.\n\n// ===== LOWERCASE = MINOR (American shorthand) =====\n// c = Cm, d = Dm, e = Em, etc.\ng           d           e           c\nThere sleeps Titania sometime of the night,\na           e           d           g\nLull'd in these flowers with dances and delight.\n\n// ===== DOMINANT 7THS & EXTENSIONS =====\n{label: verse1}\nG7          C7          D7          G7          // Dominant 7ths\nLord, what fools these mortals be!\nG9          C9          D9          G9          // 9ths\nThe course of true love never did run smooth.\nG11         C11         D13         Gmaj9       // 11ths, 13ths\nLove looks not with the eyes, but with the mind.\n\n// ===== ALTERED DOMINANTS =====\n{bpm: 100}\nG7#9        C7b9        D7#11       G7b13       // Sharp/flat extensions\nAnd therefore is wing'd Cupid painted blind.\nD7alt       G7#9#5      C7b9b13     D7#9b13     // Multiple alterations\nNor hath Love's mind of any judgement taste.\n\n// ===== DIMINISHED & AUGMENTED =====\n{label: bridge}\nGdim        Gdim7       G°          G°7         // Diminished (text & symbol)\nThe lunatic, the lover and the poet\nGaug        Gaug7       G+          G+7         // Augmented (text & symbol)\nAre of imagination all compact.\n\n// ===== HALF-DIMINISHED =====\nBm7b5       Am7b5       Bø7         Aø7         // m7b5 and ø symbol\nOne sees more devils than vast hell can hold;\nEm7b5       Dm7b5       Eø7         Dø          // Half-diminished variations\nThat is the madman.\n\n// ===== SUSPENDED & ADD CHORDS =====\n{bpm: 110}\nGsus4       Gsus2       Csus4       Dsus4       // Suspended\nThe poet's eye, in fine frenzy rolling,\nGadd9       Cadd9       Dadd9       Gadd9       // Add chords\nDoth glance from heaven to Earth.\nG(add11)    C(add9)     D(no3)      G(omit5)    // Parenthetical notation\nAnd gives to airy nothing a local habitation.\n\n// ===== MINOR-MAJOR CHORDS =====\nGmM7        CmM7        DmM7        GmM9        // Minor with major 7th\nIf we shadows have offended,\nAmM7        EmM7        BmM7        FmM7        // More minor-major\nThink but this, and all is mended.\n\n// ===== ENHARMONIC & UNICODE =====\n{label: enharmonic}\nF#m7        Gbm7        C#7         Db7         // Enharmonic equivalents\nThat you have but slumber'd here\nG♯m7        A♭maj7      D♯7         E♭7         // Unicode ♯ and ♭\nWhile these visions did appear.\n\n// ===== TEMPO MODIFIERS =====\n{bpm: +20}                                      // Relative: add 20 BPM\nG           D           Em          C\nAnd this weak and idle theme,\n\n{bpm: 75%}                                      // Percentage: 75% of current\nAm          D           G\nNo more yielding but a dream.\n\n{bpm: 2x}                                       // Multiplier: double tempo\nG*1         D*1         C*1         G*1\nGentles, do not reprehend!\n\n{bpm: 0.5x}                                     // Multiplier: half tempo\nG*2         C*2         D*2         G*2\nIf you pardon, we will mend.\n\n{bpm: reset}                                    // Reset to original (120)\nG           D           C           G\nSo, good night unto you all.\n\n// ===== TIME SIGNATURES =====\n{time: 3/4}\nG           D           Em\nGive me your hands, if we be friends,\n\n{time: 6/8}\nC           G           D\nAnd Robin shall restore amends.\n\n{time: 4/4}\n\n// ===== NC (NO CHORD / SILENCE) =====\n{label: outro}\nG           NC*2        D           NC*2        // NC = silence/rest\n(chord)     (silence)   (chord)     (silence)\n\nG*2         NC*1        D*1         G*4\nThe end... draws... near.\n\n// ===== COMPLEX FINALE =====\nGmaj7#11    Em9         Am7b5       D7#9b13\nNow the hungry lion roars,\nCmaj9#11    Bm7b5       E7alt       Am(add9)\nAnd the wolf behowls the moon.\nG/B         C           D7sus4      Gmaj7*4\nGood night... and dream of summer.\n\n{loop: outro 1}\n",
    "start": 0,
    "text_revision": 3,
